## ISS-005: Error messages leaked to clients in web-admin

### File
`/root/Redball/web-admin/server.js`

### Original (build stop handler)
```javascript
    } catch (err) {
      res.status(500).json({ error: err.message });
    }
```

### Replacement
```javascript
    } catch (err) {
      console.error('[BUILD] Failed to stop build:', err);
      res.status(500).json({ error: 'Failed to stop build' });
    }
```

### Original (releases handler)
```javascript
  } catch (err) {
    res.status(500).json({ error: err.message });
```

### Replacement
```javascript
  } catch (err) {
    console.error('[RELEASES] Failed to fetch releases:', err);
    res.status(500).json({ error: 'Failed to fetch releases' });
  }
```

### Reason
Internal `Error` messages can expose file paths, stack details, or implementation internals. Return generic client messages and log the details server-side.

### Verification
`npm test` + targeted `curl` requests to confirm `{ error: '...' }` no longer contains internal `err.message`.
